68kasm demo source
===================

`demo.s` is a small syntax and code-generation smoke test for the imported
68000 assembler.  It uses labels, `ORG`, `EQU`, `REG`, branches, `MOVEM`, and
`DC`/`DS` data directives.

Run inside platform/epoch68/emulator V7 from the directory containing `demo.s`:

	68kasm -l demo.s
	ls -l demo.h68 demo.lis
	cat demo.h68

The generated `demo.h68` is Motorola S-record text.  It is not intended to be
executed directly as a UNIX program.

For a runnable single-file program, use `hello.s`:

	68kasm hello.s
	srec2aout hello.h68 hello
	chmod 0755 hello
	hello
